{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"cinderlike-faulty-yucker","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe rebar-debug construct sweep for `fibrous-fabulous-dungbeetle` found a fourth live instance of the same centralization regression. `reconcile_helpers.py` explicitly supports standalone file-path execution and bootstraps the shared sibling loader, but `_commit_binding_store_snapshot()` unconditionally executes `from rebar_reconciler import git_adapter`. `reconcile.py` loads the helper by path under the flat key `reconcile_helpers`, so the installed in-process environment may have no top-level package.\n\n## Runtime Evidence\nA fresh process with `find_spec(\"rebar_reconciler\") is None` loaded `reconcile_helpers.py` by file path and called `_commit_binding_store_snapshot(None, real_temp_repo, \"probe\")`. It deterministically raised `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named rebar_reconciler` at `reconcile_helpers.py:200` before its documented graceful-degradation logic could run. The module-level loader contract is documented at `reconcile_helpers.py:2-15,30-50`; the flat by-path caller is `reconcile.py:60`.\n\n## Plan\n- Run rebar-debug independently to confirm the real production call path, defect legitimacy, and adapter identity requirements.\n- Add a RED oracle through the real standalone helper load and commit-back entry point.\n- Restore standalone-safe git_adapter loading with the canonical dotted cache key while preserving fail-open commit behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A standalone-loaded helper reaches the documented commit-back behavior without package-path seeding.\n- [ ] Package-context and standalone execution share one canonical git_adapter module object.\n- [ ] Commit-back failures continue to degrade to False with the documented diagnostic instead of escaping.\n- [ ] Existing helper, bridge, and reconciler suites pass.","id":"cfe1-3572-4536-49d3","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["reconciler","import","bridge"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Standalone reconcile helpers cannot import git adapter"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787047761822012001,"uuid":"3ab308ff-3207-4bdf-be38-385d9ca5d48f"}